{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Upon the land of Egypt.</b> By rights he should have stretched his hand over the sea, in order to bring the locusts, for there they are commonly found — just as we find above with the frogs, that he did not stretch his hand over the land but only over the rivers and the canals. But since Moses was destined to stretch his hand once again over the sea, HaShem did not want him to stretch his hand now over the sea."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:56:51.786187078Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}